@startuml
title LeMail - Use cases and MVP roles
left to right direction
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam shadowing false
actor Customer
actor Shipper
actor "Warehouse staff" as Warehouse
actor "Admin / dispatcher" as Admin
actor "Internal system job" as System
actor "Public viewer" as Viewer
rectangle "Parcel tracking" {
  usecase "US-01 Create parcel\nand calculate fee" as Create
  usecase "US-02 Assign pickup" as Assign
  usecase "US-03 Confirm pickup" as Pickup
  usecase "US-04 Depart / receive /\ntransfer hub" as Hub
  usecase "US-04 Dispatch last mile" as Dispatch
  usecase "US-05 Confirm delivery\nwith verified evidence" as Deliver
  usecase "US-06 Report delivery failure" as Failure
  usecase "US-06 Retry / return decision" as Retry
  usecase "US-07 Confirm return" as Return
  usecase "US-08 Cancel before pickup" as Cancel
  usecase "US-09 SLA timeout" as Lost
  usecase "Public tracking\nREST + Socket.IO" as Track
}
Customer --> Create
Customer --> Cancel
Customer --> Track
Viewer --> Track
Admin --> Assign
Admin --> Dispatch
Shipper --> Pickup
Shipper --> Hub
Warehouse --> Hub
Shipper --> Deliver
Shipper --> Failure
Shipper --> Return
System --> Assign
System --> Retry
System --> Lost
note bottom of Admin
  Prisma role = admin.
  No dispatcher login in MVP.
end note
note bottom of System
  Target job design.
  SLA/retry jobs and claim tickets
  still require B01 integration.
end note
note bottom of Deliver
  D01 prepares evidence columns.
  B01 validates and persists evidence.
  Full workflow acceptance belongs to Q01/Q03.
end note
@enduml
